lesson: 193
title: Change after buying several things
level: primary-3
stars: 0
explain: First find what each kind of thing costs in all: the price of one times how many. Then add the costs together.
explain: The change is the money given minus everything spent.
explain: With a 50-dollar note, 3 notebooks at 4 dollars and 2 pens at 6 dollars cost 12 + 12 = 24 dollars, so the change is 50 - 24 = 26 dollars.
vars: a=name j=1..3 p=2..5 x=2..12 q=2..4 y=3..15 z=5..20
let: note = (j == 1) * 20 + (j == 2) * 50 + (j == 3) * 100
let: cost = p * x + q * y
need: cost < note
answer: note - cost
exercise: {a} pays with a {note}-dollar note for {p} notebooks at {x} dollars each and {q} pens at {y} dollars each. How much change does {a.he} get?
exercise: {a} has {note} dollars. {a.He} buys {p} tickets at {x} dollars each and {q} drinks at {y} dollars each. How many dollars are left?
exercise: Mum gives {a} {note} dollars to buy {p} loaves of bread at {x} dollars each and {q} bottles of juice at {y} dollars each. How much money does {a} bring back?
exercise: {p} kg of apples cost {x} dollars a kilogram and {q} kg of pears cost {y} dollars a kilogram. {a} pays for both with {note} dollars. What change does {a.he} get?
exercise: {a} buys {p} toy cars at {x} dollars each and {q} balls at {y} dollars each and pays with {note} dollars. How many dollars of change does {a.he} receive?
test: At the first shop {a} buys {p} markers at {x} dollars each; at the second shop {a.he} buys {q} rulers at {y} dollars each. {a.He} set out with {note} dollars. How much does {a.he} have now?
test: How many dollars come back from a {note}-dollar note after paying for {q} comics at {y} dollars each and {p} puzzles at {x} dollars each?
test: {a} took {note} dollars to the market and paid {x} dollars apiece for {p} cups and {y} dollars apiece for {q} plates. How many dollars did {a.he} take home?
test: A pizza costs {x} dollars, a salad {y} dollars and a cake {z} dollars. {a} orders {p} pizzas and {q} salads and hands over {note} dollars. How much change is due?
exercise: {a} buys {p} notebooks for {x} dollars each and {q} pens for {y} dollars each, and pays with a {note}-dollar bill. How much change should {a.he} get back?
exercise: How much change does {a} get from {note} dollars after buying {q} sandwiches at {y} dollars apiece and {p} muffins at {x} dollars apiece?
exercise: At a fair in Ohio, {a} spends {x} dollars on each of {p} rides and {y} dollars on each of {q} games. {a.He} came with {note} dollars. How many dollars does {a.he} still have?
exercise: {p} books at {x} dollars each and {q} pens at {y} dollars each, paid for with {note} dollars. What is the change?
exercise: {a} goes to a shop in Toronto with {note} dollars and buys {p} packs of cards at {x} dollars a pack and {q} comics at {y} dollars a comic. How much money is left?
exercise: Dad hands {a} a {note}-dollar note to buy {p} bags of rice at {x} dollars per bag and {q} jars of honey at {y} dollars per jar. How many dollars does {a} give back to Dad?
exercise: In a café in Sydney, {a} orders {p} sandwiches at {x} dollars each and {q} juices at {y} dollars each. {a.He} pays with a note worth {note.words} dollars. How much change does {a.he} receive?
exercise: {a} has {note} dollars to spend at a craft shop. {a.He} buys {q} paintbrushes for {y} dollars each and {p} tubes of paint for {x} dollars each. How many dollars remain?
test: With {note} dollars in {a.his} pocket, {a} buys {p} T-shirts costing {x} dollars each and {q} caps costing {y} dollars each. What money is still in {a.his} pocket?
test: A {note}-dollar note pays for {p} cinema tickets at {x} dollars per ticket and {q} bags of popcorn at {y} dollars per bag. How much is handed back as change?
test: How many dollars are left from {note} after {a} buys {q} plants at {y} dollars apiece and {p} pots at {x} dollars apiece at a garden centre in Auckland?
test: {a} spent {x} dollars on every one of {p} books and {y} dollars on every one of {q} magazines. {a.He} had {note} dollars to begin with. How much has {a.he} got now?
test: A ticket to the zoo in San Diego costs {x} dollars for a child and {y} dollars for an adult. {a} pays for {p} children and {q} adults with {note} dollars. What change does {a.he} get?
test: Mum hands {a} {note} dollars. {a} buys {p} cartons of milk at {x} dollars a carton and {q} boxes of cereal at {y} dollars a box. A loaf costs {z} dollars, but {a} does not buy one. How much change does {a} bring home?
exercise: {a} paid with a {note} dollar note, {p} notebooks {x} bucks each n {q} pens {y} each. change?
exercise: got {note} dollars, bought {p} tickets at {x} each and {q} drinks at {y+1} — no wait, {y} dollars each. how much left
exercise: {a} grabbed {p} markers {x} dollar each, {q} rulers {y} dollar each, queue was like 10 people lol, paid with {note}. change how much
exercise: {a} says change is {note-x-y}. nah gotta times by how many. {p} pens at {x}, {q} pads at {y}, paid {note}. real change?
test: them pies is {x} dollar each, {a} gets {p}, plus {q} juices at {y}. hands over {note}. how much back
test: {a}'s got {note} bucks, spends on {p} comics {x} each n {q} pens {y} each, how much {a.he} got left
test: {p} cupcakes at {x} dollars, {q} lemonades at {y} dollars, paid {note}, my sis says change is {note-p*x}?? whats right
exam: It is given that {a} tenders a note of {note} dollars in payment for {p} notebooks priced at {x} dollars each and {q} pens priced at {y} dollars each. Determine the change, in dollars, due to {a}.
exam: Ascertain the sum, in dollars, remaining in the possession of {a}, who held {note} dollars prior to the purchase of {p} tickets at {x} dollars apiece and {q} beverages at {y} dollars apiece.
exam: Whereas a purchaser presents {note} dollars in settlement of an account comprising {p} articles at {x} dollars per article and {q} articles at {y} dollars per article, state the amount of change to be returned.
exam: Compute the balance, in dollars, of a sum of {note} dollars after the deduction therefrom of the total expenditure incurred in respect of {p} books at {x} dollars each and {q} maps at {y} dollars each.
exercise: Mum used to give {a} {note+20} dollars for the shopping, but since she was let go it's just a {note}-dollar note. {a} buys {p} loaves at {x} dollars each and {q} bags of rice at {y} dollars each. How much change does {a} bring back?
exercise: Grandma passed away and left {a} a {note}-dollar note 'for something nice'. {a} buys {p} comics at {x} dollars each and {q} ice creams at {y} dollars each. How many dollars are left?
test: dad's 'between jobs' so i only got a {note}, not loads. {p} pies at {x} each n {q} cokes at {y} each. how much change, and don't rip me off
